- Consolidate  general understanding of English;
- Understand the principles of teaching and learning language;
- Understand the skills needed to manage classes;
- Know language teaching methodologies.

- Have the ability and skills to use English effectively in the lectures;
- Develop independent working and teamwork skills;
- Analyze the principles of teaching and learning language.

- Apply cultural, social, psychological, linguistic and pedagogical knowledge in teaching planning, organizing and implementing their teaching in an effective and appropriate ways;
- Demonstrate good organization skills and show flexible English language teaching activities in the classroom at various levels;
- Design lectures in a clear and effective way.

- Recognize the roles of a teacher;
- Have a positive attitude towards teaching and learning;
- Be aware of the importance of teaching English as an international language, helping learners to communicate and work effectively.
